[2026/05/16 17:19:39] [DEBUG] isgsa.backend/openai: [cyan]Raw func call response: Choice(finish_reason='tool_calls', index=0, logprobs=None, message=ChatCompletionMessage(content=None, refusal=None, role='assistant', annotations=[], audio=None, function_call=None, tool_calls=[ChatCompletionMessageFunctionToolCall(id='call_xVB5fkzE61SdRV4Zey1o2b8P', function=Function(arguments='{"nl_text":"I will provide a compact experimental sketch and a self-contained Python script that loads the MovieLens 100k u.data file, validates its schema, computes the requested user-, item-, and timestamp-level statistics, and prints the results clearly. To stay aligned with recommender-systems tooling, I will use LensKit where practical for loading normalized rating data, while relying on pandas for the exact aggregation queries required by the task. The script will confirm the number of unique users and items, rank users by rating count to find the top 3 most active users, and compute the mean rating for the most active user. It will then measure co-occurrence for Items 50 and 181 by intersecting the user sets that rated each item. For timestamp validation, the code will compare observed UNIX timestamps against the expected 1997–1998 date range and report any out-of-range records without guessing. Although this is an analysis task rather than a trainable model, I will still maintain an experiment_data structure, save all derived arrays with np.save/np.savez_compressed, and print a placeholder validation_loss line to satisfy the execution requirements. Finally, I will generate a simple visualization of user activity counts and save it under the working directory with a unique filename.","code":"import os\\nworking_dir = os.path.join(os.getcwd(), \'working\')\\nos.makedirs(working_dir, exist_ok=True)\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\nimport pandas as pd\\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\\n\\nexperiment_data = {\\n    \'movielens100k_u_data\': {\\n        \'metrics\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []},\\n        \'losses\': {\'train\': [], \'val\': []},\\n        \'predictions\': [],\\n        \'ground_truth\': [],\\n        \'timestamps\': []\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n# Try to use LensKit for normalized rating loading when available/compatible.\\ndef load_with_lenskit(path):\\n    try:\\n        from lenskit.data import sparse_ratings\\n        df = pd.read_csv(path, sep=\'\\\\t\', header=None, names=[\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\', \'timestamp\'])\\n        _ = sparse_ratings(df[[\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\']])\\n        return df\\n    except Exception:\\n        return pd.read_csv(path, sep=\'\\\\t\', header=None, names=[\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\', \'timestamp\'])\\n\\ncandidate_paths = [\\n    os.path.join(os.getcwd(), \'u.data\'),\\n    os.path.join(os.getcwd(), \'ml-100k\', \'u.data\'),\\n    os.path.join(os.getcwd(), \'data\', \'u.data\'),\\n    os.path.join(os.getcwd(), \'data\', \'ml-100k\', \'u.data\'),\\n]\\n\\nfile_path = next((p for p in candidate_paths if os.path.exists(p)), None)\\nif file_path is None:\\n    raise FileNotFoundError(\'Could not find u.data in expected locations.\')\\n\\ndf = load_with_lenskit(file_path)\\ndf[\'user\'] = df[\'user\'].astype(int)\\ndf[\'item\'] = df[\'item\'].astype(int)\\ndf[\'rating\'] = df[\'rating\'].astype(float)\\ndf[\'timestamp\'] = df[\'timestamp\'].astype(np.int64)\\n\\nn_users = int(df[\'user\'].nunique())\\nn_items = int(df[\'item\'].nunique())\\n\\nuser_counts = df.groupby(\'user\').size().sort_values(ascending=False)\\ntop3 = user_counts.head(3)\\nmost_active_user = int(top3.index[0])\\nmost_active_mean_rating = float(df.loc[df[\'user\'] == most_active_user, \'rating\'].mean())\\n\\nusers_item_50 = set(df.loc[df[\'item\'] == 50, \'user\'].unique().tolist())\\nusers_item_181 = set(df.loc[df[\'item\'] == 181, \'user\'].unique().tolist())\\ncooccurrence_50_181 = int(len(users_item_50 & users_item_181))\\n\\nexpected_min = int(datetime(1997, 1, 1, tzinfo=timezone.utc).timestamp())\\nexpected_max = int(datetime(1998, 12, 31, 23, 59, 59, tzinfo=timezone.utc).timestamp())\\nout_of_range = df[(df[\'timestamp\'] < expected_min) | (df[\'timestamp\'] > expected_max)].copy()\\n\\nval_loss = float(len(out_of_range))\\nexperiment_data[\'movielens100k_u_data\'][\'losses\'][\'val\'].append({\'epoch\': 0, \'value\': val_loss})\\nexperiment_data[\'movielens100k_u_data\'][\'metrics\'][\'val\'].append({\\n    \'epoch\': 0,\\n    \'n_users\': n_users,\\n    \'n_items\': n_items,\\n    \'top3_users\': top3.index.tolist(),\\n    \'top3_counts\': top3.values.tolist(),\\n    \'most_active_mean_rating\': most_active_mean_rating,\\n    \'cooccurrence_50_181\': cooccurrence_50_181,\\n    \'n_out_of_range_timestamps\': int(len(out_of_range))\\n})\\nexperiment_data[\'movielens100k_u_data\'][\'timestamps\'].append({\'epoch\': 0, \'unix_time\': int(datetime.now(timezone.utc).timestamp())})\\n\\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, \'unique_users.npy\'), np.array([n_users]))\\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, \'unique_items.npy\'), np.array([n_items]))\\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, \'top3_active_users.npy\'), top3.index.to_numpy(dtype=np.int64))\\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, \'top3_active_user_counts.npy\'), top3.values.astype(np.int64))\\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, \'most_active_user_mean_rating.npy\'), np.array([most_active_mean_rating], dtype=np.float64))\\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, \'cooccurrence_item50_item181.npy\'), np.array([cooccurrence_50_181], dtype=np.int64))\\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, \'out_of_range_timestamps.npy\'), out_of_range[\'timestamp\'].to_numpy(dtype=np.int64))\\nnp.savez_compressed(\\n    os.path.join(working_dir, \'movielens100k_analysis_arrays.npz\'),\\n    user_counts=user_counts.to_numpy(dtype=np.int64),\\n    user_ids=user_counts.index.to_numpy(dtype=np.int64),\\n    timestamps=df[\'timestamp\'].to_numpy(dtype=np.int64),\\n    ratings=df[\'rating\'].to_numpy(dtype=np.float64)\\n)\\n\\nplt.figure(figsize=(8, 4))\\nplt.hist(user_counts.values, bins=30, color=\'steelblue\', edgecolor=\'black\')\\nplt.xlabel(\'Ratings per user\')\\nplt.ylabel(\'Number of users\')\\nplt.title(\'MovieLens100k User Activity Distribution\')\\nplt.tight_layout()\\nplt.savefig(os.path.join(working_dir, \'movielens100k_user_activity_hist.png\'), dpi=150)\\nplt.close()\\n\\nprint(f\'Unique user_ids: {n_users}\')\\nprint(f\'Unique item_ids: {n_items}\')\\nprint(\'Top 3 most active users (user_id, rating_count):\')\\nfor uid, cnt in top3.items():\\n    print((int(uid), int(cnt)))\\nprint(f\'Mean rating for most active user #{most_active_user}: {most_active_mean_rating:.6f}\')\\nprint(f\'Users who rated both Item 50 and Item 181: {cooccurrence_50_181}\')\\nprint(f\'Out-of-range timestamps count (expected 1997-1998): {len(out_of_range)}\')\\nif len(out_of_range) > 0:\\n    print(\'Sample out-of-range timestamps:\')\\n    print(out_of_range[[\'user\', \'item\', \'rating\', \'timestamp\']].head(10).to_string(index=False))\\nprint(f\'Epoch 0: validation_loss = {val_loss:.4f}\')\\n\\nnp.save(os.path.join(working_dir, \'experiment_data.npy\'), experiment_data)\\n"}', name='return_plan_and_code'), type='function')]))[/cyan]
